module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- symbolizeEffects — the pure effect-site → fresh-unknown rewrite, and the
-- composed solveSymbolic / solveFnSymbolic entries. expr-substrate Phase 14a
-- (brief: `workstreams/expr-substrate/briefs/phase-14a-symbolize-effects.md`;
-- design: `design/symbolic-execution.md`; Step-0 lock:
-- `workstreams/expr-substrate/notes/phase-14-step0.md`).
--
-- THE THESIS (locked at Step-0, GO): symbolic execution of effectful Fenel
-- code is a PURE `Expr -> Expr` rewrite + the already-shipped solver. Replace
-- each effect-call site with a fresh unknown variable (`EVar`), then hand the
-- residual predicate to `solve` / `solveFn`. The solver already treats any
-- `EVar` as a free unknown to find a witness for — so an "IO read" becomes
-- just-another-unknown with NO solver special-case, NO new `Expr` case, NO
-- native, and NO new evaluator strategy.
--
--   solve (symbolizeEffects fx .{ eq (state:getInstance "counter") 42 }) ⇒ Just 42
--                                └─ effect site → fresh EVar ─┘  no IO, no special-case
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- D-A — HOW symbolizeEffects RECOGNISES an effect-call site (the load-bearing
-- decision). In the LIVE / reified AST (pre-compilation) an effect call is a
-- normal `ECall "state:getInstance" […]` — NOT `$effect:`-marked (the
-- `$effect:` sentinel is a compile-pipeline form, never present on a reified
-- body; Step-0 §1). So a pure body keyed ONLY on `$effect:` would recognise
-- nothing live. The settled recogniser is HYBRID (option (c) primary + option
-- (a)'s recogniser folded in for free):
--   * `symbolizeEffects` takes the SET of effect fnIds explicitly (option (c)
--     — pure, zero introspection; the TS `dispatchedSolveSymbolic` wrapper
--     supplies it from a registry `requires`-walk, the SAME boundary-marshal
--     class as P13/P16's facts env — NOT a native, engine stays
--     `nativeImplsCtx === {}`), AND
--   * recognises any `$effect:<Class>:<method>`-prefixed fnId via the shipped
--     `parseEffectFnId` (option (a)'s canonical signal) so an already-effects-
--     explicit'd body works with an empty set.
-- An `ECall fnId` is an effect site ⇔ `fnId ∈ effectFnIds` OR `parseEffectFnId
-- fnId` is `Just`. The caller has full control over which fnIds symbolize; the
-- canonical sentinel works regardless. Option (b) (a Fenel-callable `requires`
-- read) is the named follow-up once an introspection read is justified — for
-- 14a it lives at the TS marshal boundary, not as a new native.
--
-- D-B — `if`/`match` PATH-SENSITIVITY is FENCED in 14a (the EVIDENCE-backed
-- call, not the brief's lean). LIFTED by the FORK DRIVER (partial-evaluator-
-- substrate Phase 3, `fork-exec.fenel`) for the PATH faces: `satSymbolicPaths`
-- (branching refutation) + `solveSymbolicPaths` (branching witness) fork the
-- residual per branch and hand each path to `satCombined`/`solve`. The 14a
-- entries below stay NON-branching (true statement, keep) — the fork faces are
-- SIBLINGS. `comprehend` does not recognise `if`, so a
-- branching predicate falls to the `SeWhere` fence. The brief's lean (i) was a
-- minimal `if c then p else q` ≡ `or (and c p) (and (not c) q)` rewrite — but
-- the boolean `and` lowers to `SeIntersect`, and `inhabit`'s intersect fold
-- is INTERVALS-ONLY (a non-interval branch ⇒ ok=false ⇒ Nothing — the Phase-5
-- fence). So `and (eq ?k 5) p` ⇒ Nothing: an if→boolean rewrite would add
-- NON-WITNESSING surface for the headline EQUALITY fragment. The real blocker
-- is enum-aware intersection (the `and`-over-enums fence), NOT the missing
-- `if` arm. Fencing `if`/`match` here and deferring the widening (enum-aware
-- `WsIntersect` first, THEN the `if` rewrite) is the honest, no-regression
-- call. `match` over `True | False` reduces to the same; richer `match` is a
-- further fence.
--
-- D-C — the composed-entry surface: `symbolizeEffects` + BOTH composed entries
-- (`solveSymbolic` predicate-Expr + `solveFnSymbolic` lambda) ship here
-- (mirrors P13/P15/P16 — body + full entry family). The `solveSymbolicAll`
-- (all satisfying reads) variant is a NAMED follow-on.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- NAMING CONSTRAINT (load-bearing — the Step-0 surprise, pinned by a test): a
-- synthetic `EVar` name must contain NO `.` — `collectFreeVars` parses a
-- dotted name as a field-access path (`?a.b` ⇒ free var `?a`), which truncates
-- the var and breaks the match against the solve variable. The site-derived
-- name uses `/` path separators and `@` to join fnId@path; `:`/`@`/`$` are all
-- safe (they appear in real effect fnIds and in `$effect:` sentinels). This is
-- a general property of `solve`, not Phase-14-specific.
--
-- SINGLE-UNKNOWN FENCE (inherited from `solve`): the symbolized predicate must
-- have EXACTLY ONE free var. A single effect site ⇒ one fresh `EVar` ⇒ solve.
-- TWO distinct sites ⇒ two distinct names (the deterministic site-path namer,
-- NO gensym counter) ⇒ 2 free vars ⇒ Nothing (solve's documented v1 fence —
-- read-to-read dependencies are the deferred `Smt` slot). For `solveFnSymbolic`
-- a lambda that ALSO references its own param yields 2 free vars (param + read)
-- ⇒ Nothing; the natural lambda shape is a `\_ -> <effectful predicate>` whose
-- only unknown is the read.
--
-- NO ENTITY DECLS (the cheapest gate class — the P5/P12/P13/P15/P16 rule): the
-- walker is structural over the registered `Expr` (7 cases); it declares NO
-- ADTs, so the entity oracle + ordered list stay UNTOUCHED and the law count
-- moves +0. Only the engine fn roster grows.
-- =========================================================================

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- symbolizeEffects — rewrite every effect-call site in an `Expr` to a fresh
-- site-named `EVar`. The public entry seeds the structural path "0" and
-- delegates to the path-threaded `symbolizeAt`.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Symbolize effects"
@description "Walk an `Expr` and rewrite every effect-call site into a fresh site-named `EVar` — turning an 'IO read' into just-another-unknown the existing solver can witness WITHOUT performing the IO. An `ECall fnId` is an effect site iff `fnId` is in the supplied `effectFnIds` set OR `parseEffectFnId fnId` is Just (the `$effect:` sentinel). The fresh var's name derives deterministically from the effect fnId + the structural path (distinct sites ⇒ distinct names ⇒ no gensym counter); the name is DOT-FREE (`/` path separators, `@` join) since a `.` would be parsed as field access by `collectFreeVars`. Everything else recurses structurally (ECall.args / ELambda.body / EMatch.scrutinee+arms / EConstruct.args / ERecord.fields); ELit/EVar pass through. Pure `Expr -> Expr` — no IO, no native, no new Expr case. The composed `solveSymbolic`/`solveFnSymbolic` feed its output to solve. expr-substrate Phase 14a."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "solve" "effect" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
symbolizeEffects : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (expr: Expr) -> Expr
symbolizeEffects effectFnIds expr = symbolizeAt effectFnIds "0" expr

-- symbolizeAt — the path-threaded recursive walker. `path` is the dot-free
-- structural path to the current node (mirrors make-effects-explicit's
-- `<path>.<suffix>` convention but with `/` separators, since the path becomes
-- part of an `EVar` name and a `.` truncates the var).
@label "symbolize: symbolizeAt"
@description "Phase 14a — the path-threaded recursive walker behind symbolizeEffects. At an effect-call site (fnId in effectFnIds OR `$effect:`-marked) emit `EVar (effectSiteName fnId path)`; else recurse structurally (ECall.args / ELambda.body / EMatch.scrutinee+arms / EConstruct.args / ERecord.fields), threading the `/`-separated structural path; ELit/EVar pass through. Mirrors substituteCaptures' structural descent (arm guard dropped, same as the sibling). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "solve" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeAt : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (path: String) -> (expr: Expr) -> Expr
symbolizeAt effectFnIds path expr =
  case expr of
    EVar { name = n } -> EVar { name = n }
    ELit { value = v } -> ELit { value = v }
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if isEffectFnId effectFnIds f
      then EVar { name = effectSiteName f path }
      else ECall { fnId = f, args = symbolizeList effectFnIds path 0 args [] }
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } ->
      ELambda { params = ps, body = symbolizeAt effectFnIds (concat path "/body") bd }
    EMatch { scrutinee = scrut, arms = arms } ->
      EMatch { scrutinee = symbolizeAt effectFnIds (concat path "/scrut") scrut, arms = symbolizeArms effectFnIds path 0 arms [] }
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args, fields = fs } ->
      EConstruct { ctor = c, args = symbolizeList effectFnIds path 0 args [], fields = fs }
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args } ->
      EConstruct { ctor = c, args = symbolizeList effectFnIds path 0 args [] }
    ERecord { fields = fs } ->
      ERecord { fields = symbolizeFields effectFnIds path fs [] }

-- isEffectFnId — an `ECall` head is an effect site iff it is in the supplied
-- effect-fnId set OR it is a `$effect:<Class>:<method>` sentinel (the D-A
-- hybrid recogniser).
@label "symbolize: isEffectFnId"
@description "Phase 14a — recognise an effect-call head: true iff `fnId` is in the supplied `effectFnIds` set (option (c), the registry `requires`-walk the TS wrapper supplies) OR `parseEffectFnId fnId` is Just (option (a), the `$effect:` sentinel). The D-A hybrid recogniser. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "effect" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
@category "engine-internal"
isEffectFnId : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (fnId: String) -> Bool
isEffectFnId effectFnIds fnId =
  if elem fnId effectFnIds then true
  else
    case parseEffectFnId fnId of
      Just p -> true
      Nothing -> false

-- effectSiteName — the DOT-FREE deterministic namer. Name = `?<fnId>@<path>`;
-- distinct sites (distinct paths) ⇒ distinct names ⇒ no gensym counter. The
-- `?` prefix is the solve-var convention; `@` joins the fnId and the path; the
-- path itself uses `/` separators. NO `.` anywhere (it would be parsed as
-- field access and truncate the var — the Step-0 surprise).
@label "symbolize: effectSiteName"
@description "Phase 14a — the dot-free deterministic site namer: `?<fnId>@<path>`. Distinct effect-call sites get distinct structural paths ⇒ distinct names ⇒ no gensym counter is threaded. The name avoids `.` (field-access truncation in collectFreeVars — the load-bearing Step-0 constraint); `?`/`@`/`:`/`$`/`/` are all safe. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
@category "engine-internal"
effectSiteName : (fnId: String) -> (path: String) -> String
effectSiteName fnId path =
  concat "?" (concat fnId (concat "@" path))

-- symbolizeList — recurse over a list of Expr children with `/`-indexed paths
-- (`<basePath>/<idx>`); threads the accumulator (the ECall.args / EConstruct.args
-- walk). Mirrors make-effects-explicit's scanIndexedExprs (dot-free paths).
@label "symbolize: symbolizeList"
@description "Phase 14a — recurse symbolizeAt over a list of Expr children with `/`-indexed structural paths (`<basePath>/<idx>`), threading the accumulator. Used for ECall.args and EConstruct.args. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeList : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (basePath: String) -> (idx: Number) -> (exprs: List Expr) -> (acc: a) -> a
symbolizeList effectFnIds basePath idx exprs acc =
  case head exprs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just h ->
      let subPath = concat basePath (concat "/" (toString idx))
      let dH = symbolizeAt effectFnIds subPath h
      let acc2 = appendItem dH acc
      case tail exprs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> symbolizeList effectFnIds basePath (idx + 1) rest acc2

-- symbolizeArms — recurse over EMatch arms with `/arm/<idx>` paths; only the
-- arm body is walked (the pattern is structural metadata). Mirrors
-- substituteCaptures' subCapArms (arm guard dropped, same as the sibling).
@label "symbolize: symbolizeArms"
@description "Phase 14a — recurse symbolizeAt over EMatch arm bodies with `/arm/<idx>` structural paths, preserving each arm's pattern (the body is the only sub-expression walked; the arm guard is dropped, mirroring substituteCaptures' subCapArms). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeArms : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (basePath: String) -> (idx: Number) -> (arms: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
symbolizeArms effectFnIds basePath idx arms acc =
  case head arms of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just arm ->
      let subPath = concat basePath (concat "/arm/" (toString idx))
      let dBody = symbolizeAt effectFnIds subPath arm.body
      let acc2 = appendItem { pattern = arm.pattern, body = dBody } acc
      case tail arms of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> symbolizeArms effectFnIds basePath (idx + 1) rest acc2

-- symbolizeFields — recurse over ERecord fields with `/<fieldname>` paths,
-- preserving each field name. Mirrors substituteCaptures' subCapFields.
@label "symbolize: symbolizeFields"
@description "Phase 14a — recurse symbolizeAt over ERecord field values with `/<fieldname>` structural paths, preserving each field name. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeFields : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (basePath: String) -> (fields: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
symbolizeFields effectFnIds basePath fields acc =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just f ->
      let subPath = concat basePath (concat "/" f.name)
      let dVal = symbolizeAt effectFnIds subPath f.value
      let acc2 = appendItem { name = f.name, value = dVal } acc
      case tail fields of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> symbolizeFields effectFnIds basePath rest acc2

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The composed entries (D-C) — siblings of solveRel / queryRel. Thin `.fenel`
-- over the SHIPPED solve / solveFn (NO new solver surface).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- solveSymbolic — `solve ∘ symbolizeEffects effectFnIds` over an already-lifted
-- predicate `Expr`. "For which read of an effect does this predicate hold?" —
-- without performing the IO. The TS `dispatchedSolveSymbolic` lifts the body +
-- supplies the effect-fnId set (registry `requires`-walk).
@label "Solve symbolic"
@description "Find a witness READ that satisfies an effectful predicate `Expr` WITHOUT performing the IO: `solve (symbolizeEffects effectFnIds expr)`. Rewrites every effect-call site (per the supplied effect-fnId set or the `$effect:` sentinel) to a fresh unknown, then hands the residual single-free-var predicate to the shipped solver. The headline `eq (state:getInstance \"counter\") 42` ⇒ Just 42, no state read. expr-substrate Phase 14a."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "solve" "effect" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
solveSymbolic : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (expr: Expr) -> Maybe a
solveSymbolic effectFnIds expr = solve (symbolizeEffects effectFnIds expr)

-- solveFnSymbolic — the lambda case: reify the marshalled Fn value, substitute
-- captures, symbolize the effect sites, then solve. reify's Err ⇒ Nothing
-- (Maybe-typed end-to-end, like solveFn). The natural shape is a
-- `\_ -> <effectful predicate>` whose only unknown is the read.
@label "Solve fn symbolic"
@description "The lambda symbolic-solve composition: reify the marshalled Fn value to its `Expr` body + captures, substitute the captures, symbolizeEffects the effect sites, then solve — finding the effect READ that satisfies the lambda-as-predicate WITHOUT performing the IO. reify's Err (bodyless / native / non-reifiable) ⇒ Nothing. The natural shape is `\\_ -> <effectful predicate>` (the only unknown is the read; a lambda that also references its own param yields 2 free vars ⇒ Nothing, solve's single-unknown fence). expr-substrate Phase 14a."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "solve" "reify" "effect" "expr-substrate" "phase-14a"
solveFnSymbolic : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (input: a) -> (ctorDefs: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> Maybe a
solveFnSymbolic effectFnIds input ctorDefs nullValue =
  case reify input ctorDefs nullValue of
    Err e -> Nothing
    Ok r -> solve (symbolizeEffects effectFnIds (substituteCaptures r.body r.captures))

-- =========================================================================
-- partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — SYMBOLIC REACH (brief:
-- `workstreams/partial-evaluator-substrate/briefs/phase-2-symbolic-reach.md`;
-- design: `design/partial-evaluation.md` §4-5 + `design/symbolic-execution.md`).
--
-- The 14a mint above is PER-SITE (distinct structural paths ⇒ distinct EVar
-- names ⇒ solve's single-unknown fence bites for a two-read predicate). Phase 2
-- lands the READ MEMORY MODEL that lets same-KEY reads share ONE unknown, and
-- the EUF refutation face that hands reads to `eufSat` as application terms —
-- lifting the two reaches the design §5 fenced (same-key multi-read for solve;
-- read-to-read refutation via congruence).
--
-- THE TWO PRESENTATIONS (Phase-5 principle, made code):
--   • To WITNESS (solve): mint effect sites into `EVar`s; VALUE-NUMBERING (same
--     class+method+eufValEq-equal args ⇒ ONE var) widens reach — `symbolizeShared`.
--   • To REFUTE (EUF): keep effect sites AS `ECall` application terms; congruence
--     needs the structure. NO mint — `satSymbolic` is the LAWFUL GATE (which
--     classes/methods/trees may be handed to `eufSat` at all).
-- Both share one soundness precondition — the MEMORY MODEL v1 (§2): the
-- value-numbered mint / the refutation gate apply only when every effect site in
-- the whole tree is a declared READ (method ∈ its class's `reads` roster) of a
-- `Symbolic`-in-scope class — i.e. NO possible write anywhere. "No write exists"
-- makes "no INTERVENING write" vacuously true for every read pair (the
-- conservative-but-sound v1; per-key interference is a §7 widening).
--
-- COMPOSED AFTER THE PE (D-A correction, in-brief): these are PURE passes over
-- the (post-PE) residual `Expr`; the PE residual preserves every effect site as a
-- residual call, so a post-PE pass sees exactly the site-set an in-walk mint
-- would. The in-walk form is deferred to the fork-driver phase.
--
-- THE SPEC currency is a plain `List { effectClass: String, reads: List String }`
-- (resolved from the scoped `Symbolic` instances at the TS marshal boundary — the
-- P13/P16 facts-env class; the explicit-arg CORES here take it as data, per the
-- 14a core-takes-data / face-resolves-data split). NO entity decls (the
-- partial-evaluate/euf entity-free precedent — law count +0).
--
-- NAMING (the value-numbered var): `?sym:<class>:<method>:<groupIndex>` — dot-free
-- (the 14a collectFreeVars constraint), and the group index is the ONLY numeric
-- part stringified (`toString`), NEVER an arg value (the eufValEq grouping makes
-- arg-value serialization unnecessary + dodges the opaque-Number `toString`
-- landmine — these entries dispatch under the PLAIN ctx where numbers stringify
-- normally). Sites failing the gate fall back to the 14a per-site `effectSiteName`.
-- =========================================================================

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Site inventory — collect every effect-call site's { fnId, typeName,
-- methodName, argTerms, hasClass } (typeName/methodName via parseEffectFnId;
-- hasClass=false for a non-sentinel fnId matched only via the effectFnIds set).
-- The traversal MIRRORS symbolizeAt EXACTLY so the memory-model gate sees the
-- same site-set the mint rewrites (EConstruct fields are NOT walked, like the
-- mint; ELambda body / EMatch arm-bodies / ECall+EConstruct args / ERecord
-- values ARE).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "symbolize: siteOf"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — decompose an effect-call site into { fnId, typeName, methodName, argTerms, hasClass }: parseEffectFnId gives (typeName, methodName) with hasClass=true for a `$effect:<Class>:<method>` sentinel; a non-sentinel fnId (matched only via the effectFnIds set) gets typeName/methodName \"\" + hasClass=false (unattributable ⇒ never value-numbered). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "effect" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symSiteOf : (fnId: String) -> (args: a) -> b
symSiteOf fnId args =
  case parseEffectFnId fnId of
    Just p -> { fnId = fnId, typeName = p.typeName, methodName = p.methodName, argTerms = args, hasClass = true }
    Nothing -> { fnId = fnId, typeName = "", methodName = "", argTerms = args, hasClass = false }

@label "symbolize: collectSites"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — collect every effect-call site in an `Expr` (as symSiteOf records), traversing structurally in EXACT mirror of symbolizeAt (ECall effect ⇒ a site else recurse args; ELambda body; EMatch scrutinee+arm-bodies; EConstruct args; ERecord field-values; EVar/ELit ⇒ none). The memory-model gate's site-set. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "effect" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symCollectSites : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (expr: Expr) -> a
symCollectSites effectFnIds expr =
  case expr of
    EVar {} -> []
    ELit {} -> []
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if isEffectFnId effectFnIds f
      then appendItem (symSiteOf f args) []
      else symCollectList effectFnIds args
    ELambda { body = bd } -> symCollectSites effectFnIds bd
    EMatch { scrutinee = scrut, arms = arms } ->
      concat (symCollectSites effectFnIds scrut) (symCollectArms effectFnIds arms)
    EConstruct { args = args } -> symCollectList effectFnIds args
    ERecord { fields = fs } -> symCollectFieldVals effectFnIds fs

@label "symbolize: collectList"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — concat symCollectSites over an Expr-child list (ECall/EConstruct args). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symCollectList : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (exprs: a) -> b
symCollectList effectFnIds exprs =
  case head exprs of
    Nothing -> []
    Just h ->
      let hereSites = symCollectSites effectFnIds h
      case tail exprs of
        Nothing -> hereSites
        Just rest -> concat hereSites (symCollectList effectFnIds rest)

@label "symbolize: collectArms"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — concat symCollectSites over EMatch arm BODIES (patterns carry no effect sites the mint touches). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symCollectArms : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (arms: a) -> b
symCollectArms effectFnIds arms =
  case head arms of
    Nothing -> []
    Just arm ->
      let hereSites = symCollectSites effectFnIds arm.body
      case tail arms of
        Nothing -> hereSites
        Just rest -> concat hereSites (symCollectArms effectFnIds rest)

@label "symbolize: collectFieldVals"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — concat symCollectSites over ERecord field VALUES. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symCollectFieldVals : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (fields: a) -> b
symCollectFieldVals effectFnIds fields =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> []
    Just f ->
      let hereSites = symCollectSites effectFnIds f.value
      case tail fields of
        Nothing -> hereSites
        Just rest -> concat hereSites (symCollectFieldVals effectFnIds rest)

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The memory model v1 — the conservative-but-sound gate. A class C is
-- "mintable" iff it is Symbolic-in-scope AND every C-site in the WHOLE tree is
-- a declared read (method ∈ reads C); PLUS a global precondition that EVERY
-- effect site is parseable (an unattributable `$effect`-less site could write
-- any store ⇒ disable value-numbering entirely). `spec` = List { effectClass,
-- reads }.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "symbolize: readsOf"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the `reads` roster for an effect class in the Symbolic spec (List { effectClass, reads }), or [] when the class is not in scope. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symReadsOf : (spec: a) -> (typeName: String) -> b
symReadsOf spec typeName =
  case head spec of
    Nothing -> []
    Just e -> if eq e.effectClass typeName then e.reads else symReadsOf (eufRest spec) typeName

@label "symbolize: classInScope"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — true when the effect class has a Symbolic instance in the spec. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symClassInScope : (spec: a) -> (typeName: String) -> Bool
symClassInScope spec typeName =
  case head spec of
    Nothing -> false
    Just e -> if eq e.effectClass typeName then true else symClassInScope (eufRest spec) typeName

@label "symbolize: isRead"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — true when methodName is a declared observationally-pure read of typeName under the spec (method ∈ reads typeName; false when the class is not in scope). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symIsRead : (spec: a) -> (typeName: String) -> (methodName: String) -> Bool
symIsRead spec typeName methodName = elem methodName (symReadsOf spec typeName)

@label "symbolize: allSitesParseable"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — true when every collected effect site is a parseable `$effect:` sentinel (hasClass). A non-parseable site is unattributable to a class ⇒ a possible write to any store ⇒ the global precondition that DISABLES value-numbering (per-site fallback for all). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symAllSitesParseable : (sites: a) -> Bool
symAllSitesParseable sites =
  case head sites of
    Nothing -> true
    Just s -> if s.hasClass then symAllSitesParseable (eufRest sites) else false

@label "symbolize: noWriteForClass"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — true when NO site of the given class is a write, i.e. every site whose typeName matches has method ∈ reads (the per-class no-write half of the memory model). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symNoWriteForClass : (spec: a) -> (sites: b) -> (typeName: String) -> Bool
symNoWriteForClass spec sites typeName =
  case head sites of
    Nothing -> true
    Just s ->
      if eq s.typeName typeName
      then (if symIsRead spec typeName s.methodName then symNoWriteForClass spec (eufRest sites) typeName else false)
      else symNoWriteForClass spec (eufRest sites) typeName

@label "symbolize: siteMintable"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — whether a single site may be value-numbered: the global no-unattributable-site precondition (parseable) AND the site is a parseable read of a Symbolic-in-scope class AND that class is write-free over the whole tree. A failing site falls back to the 14a per-site name (always sound). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symSiteMintable : (spec: a) -> (sites: b) -> (parseable: Bool) -> (site: c) -> Bool
symSiteMintable spec sites parseable site =
  if not parseable then false
  else if not site.hasClass then false
  else if not (symClassInScope spec site.typeName) then false
  else if not (symIsRead spec site.typeName site.methodName) then false
  else symNoWriteForClass spec sites site.typeName

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Value-number groups — dedup mint-eligible sites by (class, method,
-- eufValEq-equal argTerms), assigning each a sequential group index. Two reads
-- in the same group share ONE `EVar`.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "symbolize: findGroup"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the group (Just { typeName, methodName, argTerms, ix }) whose typeName+methodName match and whose argTerms are eufValEq-equal (term identity, NOT JS-loose eq), or Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "euf" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symFindGroup : (groups: a) -> (typeName: String) -> (methodName: String) -> (argTerms: b) -> Maybe c
symFindGroup groups typeName methodName argTerms =
  case head groups of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just g ->
      if and (eq g.typeName typeName) (and (eq g.methodName methodName) (eufValEq g.argTerms argTerms))
      then Just g
      else symFindGroup (eufRest groups) typeName methodName argTerms

@label "symbolize: buildGroups"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the value-number group table: scan the sites in order; each mint-eligible site whose (class, method, argTerms) is new gets a fresh sequential index. Same-key reads collapse to one group ⇒ one shared unknown. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "euf" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symBuildGroups : (spec: a) -> (sites: b) -> (parseable: Bool) -> c
symBuildGroups spec sites parseable = symBuildGroupsAcc spec sites parseable sites []

@label "symbolize: buildGroupsAcc"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the accumulator loop behind symBuildGroups: for each remaining site, append a new group { typeName, methodName, argTerms, ix = length acc } when it is mint-eligible and not already grouped. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "euf" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symBuildGroupsAcc : (spec: a) -> (allSites: b) -> (parseable: Bool) -> (rem: c) -> (acc: d) -> d
symBuildGroupsAcc spec allSites parseable rem acc =
  case head rem of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just s ->
      let acc2 =
            if symSiteMintable spec allSites parseable s
            then
              (case symFindGroup acc s.typeName s.methodName s.argTerms of
                 Just g -> acc
                 Nothing -> appendItem { typeName = s.typeName, methodName = s.methodName, argTerms = s.argTerms, ix = length acc } acc)
            else acc
      case tail rem of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just more -> symBuildGroupsAcc spec allSites parseable more acc2

@label "symbolize: sharedName"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the value-numbered var name `?sym:<class>:<method>:<groupIndex>`. Dot-free (the collectFreeVars field-access constraint); the group index is the only stringified number (never an arg value — eufValEq grouping + the opaque-Number toString landmine). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symSharedName : (typeName: String) -> (methodName: String) -> (ix: Number) -> String
symSharedName typeName methodName ix =
  concat "?sym:" (concat typeName (concat ":" (concat methodName (concat ":" (toString ix)))))

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- symbolizeShared — the value-numbered mint. Site-inventory + memory-model gate
-- + value-number groups precomputed once, then the structural walk (mirroring
-- symbolizeAt) mints a shared var for a grouped read, else falls back to the
-- 14a per-site name. The mint-context bundle `mc = { spec, sites, parseable,
-- groups }` threads the precompute.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Symbolize shared"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the VALUE-NUMBERED symbolic mint: rewrite effect-call sites to fresh `EVar`s, but same-KEY reads (same class+method+eufValEq-equal args) of a write-free Symbolic-in-scope class SHARE ONE unknown — turning `(read k) == 42 ∧ (read k) > 40` from solve's two-var fence (Nothing) into a single-unknown enum∩interval witness (Just 42). The memory model v1 (whole-tree no-write gate) makes the sharing sound. Sites failing the gate (a write present anywhere / method ∉ reads / class not Symbolic / unattributable site) fall back to the per-site 14a `effectSiteName` (always sound). `spec` = List { effectClass, reads }, resolved from the scoped `Symbolic` instances at the marshal boundary. Pure `Expr -> Expr`; composes AFTER the PE."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "solve" "effect" "euf" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
symbolizeShared : (spec: a) -> (effectFnIds: List String) -> (expr: Expr) -> Expr
symbolizeShared spec effectFnIds expr =
  let sites = symCollectSites effectFnIds expr
  let parseable = symAllSitesParseable sites
  let groups = symBuildGroups spec sites parseable
  let mc = { spec = spec, sites = sites, parseable = parseable, groups = groups }
  symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc "0" expr

@label "symbolize: symbolizeSharedAt"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the path-threaded value-numbered walker (mirrors symbolizeAt): at an effect site mint via symMintSite (shared var if grouped, else per-site fallback); else recurse structurally threading the `/`-separated path. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeSharedAt : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (mc: a) -> (path: String) -> (expr: Expr) -> Expr
symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc path expr =
  case expr of
    EVar { name = n } -> EVar { name = n }
    ELit { value = v } -> ELit { value = v }
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if isEffectFnId effectFnIds f
      then symMintSite effectFnIds mc f args path
      else ECall { fnId = f, args = symbolizeSharedList effectFnIds mc path 0 args [] }
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } ->
      ELambda { params = ps, body = symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc (concat path "/body") bd }
    EMatch { scrutinee = scrut, arms = arms } ->
      EMatch { scrutinee = symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc (concat path "/scrut") scrut, arms = symbolizeSharedArms effectFnIds mc path 0 arms [] }
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args, fields = fs } ->
      EConstruct { ctor = c, args = symbolizeSharedList effectFnIds mc path 0 args [], fields = fs }
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args } ->
      EConstruct { ctor = c, args = symbolizeSharedList effectFnIds mc path 0 args [] }
    ERecord { fields = fs } ->
      ERecord { fields = symbolizeSharedFields effectFnIds mc path fs [] }

@label "symbolize: mintSite"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — mint one effect site: if the site is mint-eligible (memory-model gate) AND its (class, method, argTerms) resolves to a value-number group, emit the shared `EVar (symSharedName …)`; else fall back to the 14a per-site `EVar (effectSiteName fnId path)`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symMintSite : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (mc: a) -> (f: String) -> (args: b) -> (path: String) -> Expr
symMintSite effectFnIds mc f args path =
  let site = symSiteOf f args
  if symSiteMintable mc.spec mc.sites mc.parseable site
  then
    (case symFindGroup mc.groups site.typeName site.methodName site.argTerms of
       Just g -> EVar { name = symSharedName site.typeName site.methodName g.ix }
       Nothing -> EVar { name = effectSiteName f path })
  else EVar { name = effectSiteName f path }

@label "symbolize: symbolizeSharedList"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — recurse symbolizeSharedAt over an Expr-child list with `/`-indexed paths, threading the mint context + accumulator (ECall/EConstruct args). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeSharedList : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (mc: a) -> (basePath: String) -> (idx: Number) -> (exprs: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
symbolizeSharedList effectFnIds mc basePath idx exprs acc =
  case head exprs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just h ->
      let subPath = concat basePath (concat "/" (toString idx))
      let dH = symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc subPath h
      let acc2 = appendItem dH acc
      case tail exprs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> symbolizeSharedList effectFnIds mc basePath (idx + 1) rest acc2

@label "symbolize: symbolizeSharedArms"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — recurse symbolizeSharedAt over EMatch arm bodies with `/arm/<idx>` paths, preserving patterns; threads the mint context. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeSharedArms : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (mc: a) -> (basePath: String) -> (idx: Number) -> (arms: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
symbolizeSharedArms effectFnIds mc basePath idx arms acc =
  case head arms of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just arm ->
      let subPath = concat basePath (concat "/arm/" (toString idx))
      let dBody = symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc subPath arm.body
      let acc2 = appendItem { pattern = arm.pattern, body = dBody } acc
      case tail arms of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> symbolizeSharedArms effectFnIds mc basePath (idx + 1) rest acc2

@label "symbolize: symbolizeSharedFields"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — recurse symbolizeSharedAt over ERecord field values with `/<fieldname>` paths, preserving field names; threads the mint context. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symbolizeSharedFields : (effectFnIds: List String) -> (mc: a) -> (basePath: String) -> (fields: b) -> (acc: c) -> c
symbolizeSharedFields effectFnIds mc basePath fields acc =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just f ->
      let subPath = concat basePath (concat "/" f.name)
      let dVal = symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc subPath f.value
      let acc2 = appendItem { name = f.name, value = dVal } acc
      case tail fields of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> symbolizeSharedFields effectFnIds mc basePath rest acc2

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The composed WITNESS entry + the detailed { residual, mintTable } face.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Solve symbolic shared"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — `solve (symbolizeShared spec effectFnIds expr)`: the value-numbered symbolic solve. The memory model collapses same-key reads to ONE unknown, so `(read k) == 42 ∧ (read k) > 40` witnesses `Just 42` (enum∩interval over the shared var) where the per-site 14a mint returns Nothing (two vars). `spec` = List { effectClass, reads }."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "solve" "effect" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
solveSymbolicShared : (spec: a) -> (effectFnIds: List String) -> (expr: Expr) -> Maybe b
solveSymbolicShared spec effectFnIds expr = solve (symbolizeShared spec effectFnIds expr)

@label "symbolize: mintTable"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — project the value-number groups to a mint table `List { varName, typeName, methodName, argTerms }` (varName ⇒ the read it stands for; `var` is a reserved keyword) — the future fork-driver + Nelson-Oppen currency (plain records, no entity). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symMintTable : (groups: a) -> b
symMintTable groups =
  case head groups of
    Nothing -> []
    Just g ->
      let row = { varName = symSharedName g.typeName g.methodName g.ix, typeName = g.typeName, methodName = g.methodName, argTerms = g.argTerms }
      case tail groups of
        Nothing -> appendItem row []
        Just rest -> concat (appendItem row []) (symMintTable rest)

@label "Symbolize shared detailed"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the detailed value-numbered mint over an (already-PE'd, lifted) residual `Expr`: returns `{ residual, mintTable }` where mintTable maps each shared var to its { typeName, methodName, argTerms }. The `peSymbolic` composition (PE via the existing seam → this) yields the fork-driver / Nelson-Oppen input currency without a new PE surface."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "solve" "effect" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
symbolizeSharedDetailed : (spec: a) -> (effectFnIds: List String) -> (expr: Expr) -> b
symbolizeSharedDetailed spec effectFnIds expr =
  let sites = symCollectSites effectFnIds expr
  let parseable = symAllSitesParseable sites
  let groups = symBuildGroups spec sites parseable
  let mc = { spec = spec, sites = sites, parseable = parseable, groups = groups }
  let residual = symbolizeSharedAt effectFnIds mc "0" expr
  { residual = residual, mintTable = symMintTable groups }

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- satSymbolic — the REFUTATION face (Deliverable C), WIDENED at decide-substrate
-- Phase 6 from EUF-only to the Nelson-Oppen combined theory (`satCombined`).
-- Reads handed to the theory AS application terms (congruence needs the
-- structure — NO mint), plus their order atoms (lte/lt/gte/gt) so order
-- constraints over reads refute too. The LAWFUL GATE is unchanged: every effect
-- site in the predicate must be a declared READ of a Symbolic-in-scope class
-- (⇒ no writes, no unknown classes) — the Phase-5 soundness contract
-- ("congruence over effectful call sites is the CALLER's modeling
-- responsibility") made data. Any violation ⇒ Nothing (honest). The ambient
-- `noDecideWhere` decider arm STILL fences all `$effect:` heads defensively (no
-- memory model) ⇒ decideEmpty stays Nothing on the same SeWhere; THIS is the
-- caller that lifts that fence lawfully.
--
-- VERDICT: `Just false` (unsat — a genuine refutation over EVERY store) / else
-- `Nothing` (combined-sat does NOT certify satisfiability of the full mixed
-- predicate — dropped conjuncts + finite domains; the Phase-5 honesty verbatim).
-- Never `Just true`.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "symbolize: allSitesScopedReads"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 — the lawful-gate predicate: true iff EVERY collected effect site is a parseable declared read (hasClass ∧ class ∈ spec ∧ method ∈ reads class) — i.e. no writes, no unknown/unattributable classes anywhere. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "symbolize" "euf" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
symAllSitesScopedReads : (spec: a) -> (sites: b) -> Bool
symAllSitesScopedReads spec sites =
  case head sites of
    Nothing -> true
    Just s ->
      if and s.hasClass (and (symClassInScope spec s.typeName) (symIsRead spec s.typeName s.methodName))
      then symAllSitesScopedReads spec (eufRest sites)
      else false

@label "Sat symbolic"
@description "partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 2 (WIDENED decide-substrate Phase 6) — the Nelson-Oppen refutation face over an effectful predicate `Expr`: the LAWFUL GATE (every effect site is a declared read of a Symbolic-in-scope class — no writes, no unknown classes; any violation ⇒ Nothing) then hand the and-spine's MIXED atoms (noWhereAtoms — eq/neq PLUS lte/lt/gte/gt) to `satCombined` with the read sites INTACT as `ECall` application terms (congruence needs the structure). `read(a)==1 ∧ read(b)==2 ∧ a==b` ⇒ Just false (EUF-unsat over the reads-as-applications, zero IO); `read(k)==1 ∧ read(k)==2` ⇒ Just false; `read(a) ≤ read(b) ∧ read(b) ≤ read(a) ∧ f(read a) ≠ f(read b)` ⇒ Just false (the order theory derives read a = read b, EUF refutes); a `write` site anywhere ⇒ Nothing; a class not declared Symbolic ⇒ Nothing. Just false = refuted over EVERY store; else Nothing (never Just true — dropped conjuncts + finite domains). The ambient decideEmpty still fences the same SeWhere to Nothing (the decider has no memory model); this face is its lawful caller. `spec` = List { effectClass, reads }."
@tags "engine" "symbolize" "euf" "solve" "prover" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-2"
satSymbolic : (spec: a) -> (effectFnIds: List String) -> (pred: Expr) -> Maybe Bool
satSymbolic spec effectFnIds pred =
  let sites = symCollectSites effectFnIds pred
  if not (symAllSitesScopedReads spec sites) then Nothing
  else
    let atoms = noWhereAtoms pred
    case satCombined atoms.eqs atoms.neqs atoms.ltes atoms.lts of
      Just false -> Just false
      _ -> Nothing
